<h2>Chapter 5: Insurance Industry Relationships: The Preferred Vendor Playbook</h2>
<h3>Why Insurance Relationships Matter More Than Google Ads</h3>
<p>Ed Cross, former president of the Restoration Industry Association, put it bluntly: "The restoration companies that thrive long-term are the ones with deep insurance relationships, not the ones spending the most on Google Ads."</p>
<p>Here is the math:</p>
<ul>
<li>Insurance-sourced work accounts for <strong>20-50% of revenue</strong> for established restoration companies</li>
<li>A single adjuster relationship can generate <strong>12-30 jobs per year</strong></li>
<li>Companies with 6-12 preferred vendor relationships can generate <strong>$2M-$10M+ annually</strong> without consumer ad spend</li>
<li>Preferred vendor program leads cost <strong>$0 in direct marketing spend</strong> — the carrier dispatches you</li>
</ul>
<p>Building insurance relationships is not networking. It is a systematic, repeatable process.</p>
<h3>Understanding the Insurance Ecosystem</h3>
<p>To market to insurance professionals, you must understand their world. Here are the key players:</p>
