<h4>Tier 4: Direct Carrier Programs</h4>
<p>Major carriers operate their own preferred vendor networks:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>State Farm</strong> — Select Service / Premier Service</li>
<li><strong>Allstate</strong> — Good Hands Repair Network</li>
<li><strong>USAA</strong> — Preferred Contractor Program</li>
<li><strong>Liberty Mutual</strong> — Master Service Agreement</li>
<li><strong>Travelers, Farmers, Nationwide</strong> — Various programs</li>
</ul>
<p>Direct carrier programs are the most difficult to enter but offer the highest volume. Requirements include all TPA credentials plus:<br />
- Demonstrated capacity (multiple crews, equipment inventory)<br />
- Catastrophe response capability (deploying teams to disaster zones)<br />
- Customer satisfaction scores above network averages<br />
- Financial stability (carrier may review financials)</p>
<h3>The Preferred Vendor Application Process</h3>
<p><strong>Step 1: Credential audit</strong><br />
- Verify all IICRC certifications are current<br />
- Confirm insurance coverage meets minimums<br />
- Ensure Xactimate licenses are active<br />
- Compile technician certification records</p>
<p><strong>Step 2: Operational documentation</strong><br />
- Write standard operating procedures for emergency response<br />
- Document SLA compliance tracking<br />
- Create quality control checklists<br />
- Build customer satisfaction measurement system</p>
<p><strong>Step 3: Application submission</strong><br />
- Complete carrier/TPA application forms<br />
- Submit credential documentation<br />
- Provide references from past insurance work<br />
- Pass background and financial checks</p>
<p><strong>Step 4: Trial period</strong><br />
- Receive limited dispatch volume<br />
- Demonstrate compliance with all requirements<br />
- Maintain customer satisfaction scores<br />
- Pass quality audits</p>
<p><strong>Step 5: Full program participation</strong><br />
- Receive regular dispatch volume<br />
- Maintain ongoing compliance<br />
- Participate in continuing education<br />
- Renew credentials annually</p>
