<h3>Documentation Excellence: The Hidden Marketing Tool</h3>
<p>Your documentation is your reputation in the insurance world. Sloppy documentation creates friction. Friction creates blacklists.</p>
<p><strong>Documentation standards that impress adjusters:</strong></p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Xactimate estimates</strong> — Line items match adjuster format exactly. No custom line items without justification</li>
<li><strong>Moisture logs</strong> — Daily readings with equipment placement maps, per IICRC S500 standards</li>
<li><strong>Photo documentation</strong> — Before, during, after. Every room. Every angle. Timestamped</li>
<li><strong>Drying records</strong> — Equipment readings, psychrometric data, drying goals achieved</li>
<li><strong>Scope narratives</strong> — Clear explanations of why work was necessary</li>
<li><strong>Direct portal uploads</strong> — Submit through carrier-approved platforms (XactAnalysis, Sedgwick viaOne, Crawford ClaimsCenter)</li>
</ol>
<p>Companies with documentation excellence get faster approvals, fewer disputes, and more referrals. It is marketing disguised as operations.</p>
